[21.232648, "o", "\u001b[1mkv-cli\u001b[0m \u001b[1;36maudit\u001b[0m  \u001b[2m.kovallent.yaml\u001b[0m  1 file\r\n  \u001b[2m·\u001b[0m contract \u001b[1m4bc0fc3192e4e992\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m·\u001b[0m functions: 1 in scope, 0 framework-exempt, 0 user-exempt, 0 out of scope\r\n\r\n\u001b[4mjobs/load_orders.py\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m   3\u001b[0m  \u001b[1;31merror\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mKV002\u001b[0m  `DB_PASSWORD` is assigned a hardcoded literal\r\n        \u001b[2mvalue \"s3…\" (<redacted>, 20 chars) - load it from the environment or a secret store\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m   4\u001b[0m  \u001b[1;33mwarning\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mKV003\u001b[0m  environment-specific identifier (object_store_uri)\r\n        \u001b[2m`s3://acme-prod-landing/orders/` should vary by environment\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m   7\u001b[0m  \u001b[1;31merror\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mKV001\u001b[0m  `run_load` is missing contract parameter `target_environment`\r\n        \u001b[2mexpected signature to declare `target_environment: str = \"dev\"`\u001b[0m\r\n        \u001b[2min scope: name matches applies_to.name_patterns \"run_*\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m   7\u001b[0m  \u001b[1;33mwarning\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mKV001\u001b[0m  `run_load` is missing contract parameter `dry_run`\r\n        \u001b[2mexpected signature to declare `dry_run: bool = False`\u001b[0m\r\n        \u001b[2min scope: name matches applies_to.name_patterns \"run_*\"\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2m·\u001b[0m files: 1 failing, 0 warning-only, 0 clean, 0 skipped\r\n\u001b[1;31mFAIL\u001b[0m 2 errors, 2 warnings\r\n\u001b[2mrun `kv-cli fix` to apply the standard fixes\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mrun `kv-cli explain KV001` for what a rule checks and how to fix it\u001b[0m\r\n"]
